# Samples layout

`.love` samples live under [`samples/`](../../samples/). They exercise features end-to-end (CLI, integration tests, manual checks). They **do not** replace AUnit tests (see testing-aunit).

## Required layout

- **Never** put a `.love` file directly in `samples/` (no `samples/Foo.love`).
- Always place samples in a **feature subfolder**: `samples/<feature>/…`.
- `<feature>` is a short kebab-case or single-word name for the main capability (e.g. `program`, `module`).
- Reuse an existing feature folder when the sample belongs to that feature; create a new folder only for a new feature group.
- Keep the sample `program` / `module` identifier identical to the `.love` basename (excluding the extension; dots allowed in module names, e.g. `Foo.Bar.love`).

```text
# BAD
samples/Hello.love
samples/Empty.love

# GOOD
samples/program/Hello.love
samples/module/Empty.love
samples/module/Foo.Bar.love
```

## When adding samples

- For every new user-facing language or CLI feature that needs a sample, add at least one `.love` under the matching `samples/<feature>/` folder in the same change.
- Prefer the smallest valid surface that demonstrates the feature.
- Update [`docs/samples.md`](../../docs/samples.md) and any docs/CLI/integration paths that cite the sample.
